WEBVTT

00:00:00.687 --> 00:00:03.906
Every agent works in its own git worktree:

00:00:03.906 --> 00:00:06.359
a fresh checkout of the project.

00:00:06.359 --> 00:00:14.944
FlightDeck links your dot env file into it, but anything else git doesn't track stays behind, like node_modules.

00:00:15.328 --> 00:00:18.578
Open a terminal in the new worktree, and look.

00:00:21.088 --> 00:00:26.150
The dot env file is there, but no dependencies, so the app won't start.

00:00:26.778 --> 00:00:32.180
Hooks fix that. Each project has a hooks file in its dot flightdeck folder.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:38.806
Commands under worktree created run in every new worktree, as soon as FlightDeck creates it.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.488
Here, install the dependencies.

00:00:43.101 --> 00:00:44.865
Now start another agent.

00:00:55.841 --> 00:01:00.020
The hook installed its dependencies, so the app starts right away.

00:01:15.364 --> 00:01:19.855
The hooks file is gitignored, so your hooks only run on your machine.

00:01:19.855 --> 00:01:24.606
To share them with your team, take it out of the gitignore and commit it.
